# Canvas executable lockdown

- `/canvas` is the only official current Canvas route; `/canvas-v4` and preview routes must remain absent.
- `/canvas-legado` remains available until an explicit deletion patch.
- `src/app/canvas` only routes, lays out and composes Server Components.
- The interactive Canvas is a dynamically loaded Client island inside the Canvas feature.
- `<ReactFlow />` is the only Canvas renderer. Custom cards are React Flow nodes with real `<Handle />` ports; causal relations are custom React Flow edges.
- Manual SVG connection layers, route-owned state engines and duplicate causal rules are forbidden.
- `evaluateCanvasConnection` is the single causal policy and invalid actions must not mutate state.
- Each component, hook, test, adapter and mock remains with its owner. `shared` cannot import private Canvas implementation.
- Component files may not exceed 260 lines; controller hooks may not exceed 360 lines without an approved contract migration.
- Persistence crosses explicit application and repository contracts. Browser storage and `window.location` are forbidden.
- The Canvas visual skin is protected by hash and by the external before/after Playwright screenshot in patch validation.
- Run `npm run validate:canvas:release` before commit or merge.
